$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(4-((4-Ethylpiperazin-1-yl)methyl)-3-(trifluoromethyl)-
phenyl)-3-iodo-4-methylbenzamide (32). To a stirred solution of
3-iodo-4-methylbenzoic acid 31 (262 mg, 1 mmol) and aniline 29 (430 mg,
1.5 mmol) in 10 mL of dichloromethane were added HATU (570 mg, 1.5 mmol),
DMAP (185 mg, 1.5 mmol), and DIEA (520 μL, 3 mmol). The reaction mixture
was allowed to stand for 24 h at room temperature, then diluted with
ethyl acetate and washed with water and brine. The organic phase was
dried over Na2SO4, filtered, then concentrated and purified with column
chromatography (dichloromethane/ methanol 20:1). The title compound as a
yellow solid (480 mg, 90%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.35 (br, 1H), 8.33
(s, 1H), 7.91 (m, 2H), 7.80 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (d, J = 9.0, 1H),
7.32 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 3.66 (s, 2H), 3.00−2.58 (m, 8H), 2.71 (m, 2H),
2.48 (s, 3H), 1.26 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H). MS (ESI) m/z 532 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
