$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 10: N,N-Diisopropylethylamine (0.057ml, 0.33 mmol) was added to
a solution of compound 9 (24 mg, 0.0658 mmol),
(R)-(+)-1-Boc-3-aminopyrrolidine (12 mg, 0.0658 mmol), and
O-(benzotriazol-1-yl)-N,N,N’,N’-tetramethyluronium tetrafluorobotate (32
mg, 0.099 mmol) in dichloromethane (2mL). The resulting solution was
stirred at rt for 2h. The reaction mixture was concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude product was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane-ethyl acetate mixture. Compound 10 as a white
solid (40 mg, 89%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 7.99 (s, 1H), 7.88-7.84 (m,
2H), 7.58-7.37 (m, 7H), 7.24 (d, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz), 6.97-6.90 (m, 1H), 6.72
(s, 1H), 6.42 (m, 1H), 4.80 (s, 2H), 4.45-4.43 (m, 1H), 3.63-3.59 (m,
1H), 3.35-3.31 (m, 2H), 3.04 (m, 1H), 2.39 (s, 3H), 2.12-2.09 (m, 1H),
1.76 (m, 1H)1.37 (s, 9H).
