$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure I (for cat.1, cat .3 and
cat.5) N-Boc-amino acid (10 mmol) was dissolved in THF (25 mL) and cooled
in an ice bath. NMM (10 mmol) and ethyl chloroformate ( 10 mmol) were
added to the aboved cooled solution and stirred for 30min. The resulting
mixture was treated with sulfonyl hydrazide (1.2 eq, 12mmol) at 0 °C.
After 2h the solvent THF was evaporated and the residue was dissolved in
DCM (200 mL). Then the DCM layer was washed with hydrogen chloride
solution (2M, 60×3 mL) and brine subsequently. The solvent was dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated in vacuum. The crude product which could
be used in next step directly. The above crude product was dissolved in
DCM (50 mL) and cooled in an ice bath. TFA (100 mmol) was added and
stirred overnight. The resulting mixture was evaporated in vacuum and the
residue was dissolved in DCM (100 mL). Then the DCM layer was washed with
Na2CO3 saturated solution (30×3 mL) and a lot of precipitate appeared in
the cases of cat.1 and cat.3. The precipitate was filtered and washed
with water and ice-cooled ethanol subsequently. The obtained solid was
dried in vacuum furthermore and the obtained product could be used in
reaction as catalyst directly. In the case of cat.5, the DCM layer was
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and removed in vacuum. The crude product was
further purified by flash chromatography ( DCM/Methanol = 20/1 ).
(S)-N'-(2-amino-3-phenylpropanoyl)-4-(trifluoromethyl)benzenesulfonohydrazide
(cat.3): white solid in 89 % yield. M.p. 228-231 °C. [α]D 20 +6.5 (c =
1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400MHz, d6-DMSO): δ 8.00-7.95 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, J =
12.4 Hz, 4H), 7.37-7.28 (m, 3H), 7.20-7.18 (m, 2H), 3.94-3.91 (t, J = 6.8
Hz, 1H) 2.98-2.93 (dd, J = 2.8 Hz, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H), 2.83-2.78 (dd, J =
7.6 Hz, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, d6-DMSO): δ 168,
158.89-157.96 (q, J = 31 Hz), 143.14, 134.55, 133.23-132.27 (q, J = 32.1
Hz), 129.54, 128.67-128.62 (d, J = 5.4 Hz), 127.25, 126.20-126.16 (J =
3.6 Hz), 124.93-115.77 (q, J = 270.9 Hz); IR (film, ν/cm-1 ): 3034, 1672,
1502, 1406, 1325, 1173, 1063, 841, 719; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C16H16N3O3SF3 [M+H]+ 388.0943, found 388.0935.
