$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)acetate (INT-A): HATU (0.36 g, 0.96
mmol) and DIPEA (0.25 mL, 1.4 mmol) were added to a solution of
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (0.27 g, 0.80 mmol) in DMF (2 mL). After
10 min, methyl 2-aminoacetate HCl salt (0.1 g, 0.80 mmol) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture
was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated, and purified by
silica gel column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc in hexanes). (S)-Methyl
2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)-3-((tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino)propanoate:
The title compound was synthesized similarly to INTA using (S)-methyl
2-amino-3-((tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino)propanoate HCl salt (242 mg, 0.95
mmol) and 4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (319 mg, 0.95 mmol). The
reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated,
and purified by silica gel column chromatography (0-50% EtOAc in
hexanes). The product as a clear oil (453 mg, 89%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 8.74 (d, J=7.78 Hz, 1 H) 8.29 (s, 1 H) 7.70 (s, 1 H)
7.31-7.50 (m, 10 H) 7.09-7.16 (m, 1 H) 5.34 (s, 4 H) 4.43-4.57 (m, 1 H)
3.59-3.69 (m, 3 H) 3.37-3.50 (m, 2 H) 1.29-1.38 (m, 9 H). ESI-MS m/z:
536.2 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Efficacious Pseudomonas aeruginosa-Targeted
Siderophore-Conjugated Monocarbams by Application of a Semi-mechanistic
Pharmacokinetic/Pharmacodynamic Model
